# Optional. Everything works without any of these.

# Google Apps Script endpoint that receives pilot-access requests from the marketing page.
# VITE_SHEET_ENDPOINT=

# Optional language layer (translation of a person's own check-in note only).
# AI never creates plan content or touches the safety rules. If unset or failing, the
# original wording is saved and approved fixed templates are used.
# Contract: POST { text, source, target } -> { translation: string }
# VITE_LANGUAGE_API_URL=

# Optional Comeback Coach wording (Groq, free tier). The model only rewrites an already-validated,
# structured suggestion as kind wording. Risk scores, safety limits and the allowed actions are
# deterministic and never depend on it. If unset, rate-limited or failing, fixed templates are used.
#
# 1) Browser-visible: the URL of the proxy. It contains no secret.
#    Local dev:   VITE_COACH_API_URL=/api/coach-explain   (served by the Vite dev server)
#    Production:  VITE_COACH_API_URL=https://<your-host>/api/coach-explain
# VITE_COACH_API_URL=
#
# 2) SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Put this in .env.local (git-ignored) for local dev, or in your host's
#    environment-variable settings for the serverless function in api/coach-explain.ts.
#    Never prefix it with VITE_, or it would be bundled into the public site.
#    Free key: https://console.groq.com/keys
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# Optional: several comma-separated keys; the next one is tried when one hits its free rate limit.
# GROQ_API_KEYS=

# Accounts (Supabase). The URL and PUBLISHABLE key are public by design: row-level security protects the data.
# Without them the app hides the sign-in option and Guest / Local modes work as before.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# Optional: show a "type the code" box on the sign-in screen (needs a custom email template containing {{ .Token }}).
# VITE_AUTH_CODE_ENTRY=1
#
# Migrations and tests only (scripts/db-run.mjs). LOCAL ONLY, never VITE_ and never committed:
# SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Never put secrets in VITE_* variables: they are bundled into the public site.
